design

# DELIBERATE: `docs` is NOT here, and this is the whole of why. `next.config.ts` traces
# `docs/brief.md` into `/api/assistant`, so the file has to be in the build context for the
# standalone build to find it. Excluded here, the trace found nothing, the shipped image carried
# no brief, and `readBrief` (`src/lib/assistant/brief.ts`) returns '' rather than throwing — so
# every reply in production was written without the Product, Users and Glossary sections the
# README says they carry, and nothing said so.
#
# The runtime stage copies only `.next/standalone`, `.next/static` and `public`, so the rest of
# `docs/` still does not ship. Exactly one file does, and it is the one that was traced.
#
# Secrets, mirrored from `.gitignore`'s own secrets block. `COPY . .` puts the whole context in
# the build stage, and `.env.local` is a live credential: it does not reach the runtime stage
# either, for the same reason, but a credential in a build layer is still a credential in an
# image sitting on a registry.
.env
.env*.local
*.local

# DELIBERATE: `**/`, not a bare `.DS_Store`. A .dockerignore pattern without a slash matches at the
# context root only, and the runtime stage copies the whole of `public/` in, so the macOS metadata
# file that reaches a deployment is the one sitting beside the brand assets.
**/.DS_Store
